+# Deferred-origin observation contract (staged)
+
+Status: proposed sender/receiver read contract extending section 7 for draft PR4077,
+**pending independent review, not implemented or advertised by the serving Board.**
+The approved spec requires observation but does not specify this new read surface.
+This document does not enable replay, migrate
+slots, add a writer, or authorize cancellation. The approved post-collection design
+sections 4, 6 and 7 remain normative.
+
+## Why a separate read is needed
+
+A final `deferred` replay verdict names `{task, origin}` and establishes that status
+was handed to the Board's existing bounded origin queue. It is not current queue
+membership, a current-row snapshot, or proof that the requested status applied.
+The slot retains only its last verdict and later independent operations replace it.
+Core must acknowledge transport without replaying that row, permit later origin
+delivery, and separately observe unresolved status custody.
+
+## Capability and authenticated read
+
+The serving Board's existing replay capability response must advertise
+`deferred_observation: "origin_pending1"` only when the same serving implementation
+supports this read. Missing/unknown capability never means an empty queue. The
+sender must refuse to settle a deferred verdict without durable semantic custody;
+it must not fall back to legacy transport or infer resolution from a receipt.
+
+Proposed route (future, not an existing production endpoint):
+
+`GET /v2/boards/{board}/replay/deferred?task={percent-encoded-task-id}`
+
+Use the existing Board enrollment authentication and Board-read authorization.
+Identity fields are server-derived, never caller-supplied. A successful reply is:
+
+```json
+{
+  "protocol": "origin_pending1",
+  "board_incarnation": "<immutable Board identity>",
+  "gateway_principal": "<authenticated caller principal>",
+  "task": "<exact requested task id>",
+  "complete": true,
+  "entries": [
+    {
+      "origin": "<event uid>",
+      "hlc": "<retained entry HLC>",
+      "gateway": "<retained entry gateway id, not a principal attestation>",
+      "run": null,
+      "status": "done",
+      "evidence_sha256": "<64 lowercase hex characters>"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+Read the requested task's **entire** `origin_pending:<task>` value in one synchronous
+read snapshot, normalizing the existing singleton compatibility form to an array.
+Return every entry, including entries from other gateways; never filter to only the
+caller's entries and imply that the task is empty. There are at most 16 distinct
+origins per task, so this route has no pagination or truncation. `run` is the retained
+run UID or null. `evidence_sha256` is SHA256 of RFC8785 canonical UTF-8 JSON of the
+complete stored queue entry `{status, hlc, origin, gateway, run, receipt}`. The
+`receipt` carries source-retention evidence used by deferred custody release; those
+fields remain stored unchanged and need not be disclosed in this diagnostic reply.
+The fingerprint is an evidence-change token, not authorization or an operation ID.
+Do not equate the historical `gateway` display ID with an immutable principal.
+
+A complete empty array establishes only **absence from the current queue**. It does
+not distinguish application, supersession or deletion and must never mark the
+requested status applied, overwrite a pulled task, advance sync_version, or clear an
+unrelated rejection. A missing task with no queue also returns complete empty state;
+a missing task with retained entries still returns those entries.
+
+Reject malformed requests normally. Corrupt/over-bound stored state, missing RPC
+on an older Durable Object, authentication/identity mismatch, partial data and
+storage/network failures are unavailable observations, never empty results. This
+read must not expire leases, resolve entries, sweep, publish feed/events, acknowledge
+transport, or change any business state. Capability and read availability are checked
+on the serving Board, not inferred from the outer Worker's health/version.
+
+## Sender custody and bounded diagnostics
+
+On a final deferred verdict, atomically preserve the task/origin reference and the
+observed handoff separately from current-row sync state, settle the journal, and
+prune only transport custody. Validate the reference against the issued frozen
+source; do not replace it with a newer local origin. Do not mark the deferred status
+successful. Non-status fields may already have settled under normal arbitration;
+current-row hydration remains a separate authenticated read.
+
+Maintain at most 16 active origin diagnostic records **per task**, keyed by
+Board incarnation, task and origin, not an ever-growing per-operation ledger.
+Only a complete validated response may replace that task's observed membership.
+Preserve the previous visible records on unavailable observations. A queue-entry
+fingerprint change resets its diagnostic episode; unchanged evidence deduplicates
+an escalation across reopen/restart. Observed absence retires only the active
+queue diagnostic, without converting the recorded deferred outcome into success
+or changing current-row status. Resolution reason remains unknown; current-row
+reconciliation is separate, and there is no permanent per-operation outcome ledger.
+No TTL silently discards unresolved custody. If a new handoff would exceed the
+local 16-record bound, preserve its issued transport custody while first obtaining
+a complete fresh observation to retire stale membership. Only an inconsistent
+complete observation (or unavailable reconciliation) may leave an explicit local
+reconciliation fault; this is not a receiver overflow rejection or permission to
+evict another record, fabricate success, or replay the transport under a new ID.
+
+Poll outside writer transactions. Bind the read response to the journal identity
+and exact task, validate distinct origins and all fields before any local mutation,
+then persist observation changes atomically. Do not block independent stream work
+or origin-event delivery while unresolved diagnostics exist. Discovery must cover
+all tracked tasks fairly with a durable bounded rotating cursor, not repeatedly
+poll only the first prefix. A legacy stored queue discovered by this route is an
+observation, not certification of capture provenance or transport success.
+
+After 300 seconds of reachable observation of unchanged unresolved evidence, emit
+one actionable owner diagnostic naming task, origin and evidence fingerprint. Do
+not count offline time, process downtime or a failed/invalid read as reachable time.
+Use successive successful observation intervals capped by a 60-second sampling
+gap; a larger gap or restart begins a new baseline without adding the gap. Retain
+already accumulated reachable time and emitted-episode identity durably. Failure
+resets only the sampling baseline, never the obligation or its accumulated time.
+Observation clock regression adds no time. This is conservative diagnostic timing,
+not proof of continuous service availability between samples. It creates no repair,
+new op identity, cancellation request, force-delete, or authority to resolve custody.
+The existing owner delivers the dependency or an authorized superseding lifecycle
+operation; separate business-control review is required for explicit cancellation.
+
+## Required implementation proof (still open)
+
+Receiver: real authenticated HTTP/DO tests for empty/current/full-16 queues,
+singleton compatibility, other-gateway entries, missing task with retained custody,
+corrupt/overflow state, immutable caller/Board identity, old-DO RPC refusal, and
+unchanged whole business/feed/lease state after reads. Fingerprint changes must
+cover status, gateway, run and source receipt as well as origin/HLC.
+
+Sender: row-before-origin and origin-before-row through actual push, exact final
+handoff recovery after restart/reply loss, rollback of local semantic custody and
+journal together, no resend/version success, independent and origin-event progress,
+validated complete read versus unavailable/malformed/partial/wrong-identity replies,
+16-origin bound, evidence-change and disappearance without fabricated success,
+restart/offline/gap/regressing-clock timing, deduplicated five-minute escalation and
+fair task rotation. Controlled future-contract fixtures must be labelled as such;
+they are not live observations or cross-repository integration proof.
